@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = null;
}
<section class="hero">
  <div class="pitch">
    <h1>Less explaining. More playing.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Flag football plays young kids can follow. On game day, pick a play on your
      tablet, turn it toward the team, and show them what to do. Tap a player to
      walk through that kid's job, one step at a time. At practice, use the same
      board to teach the plays before you need to call them.</p>
    <p><strong>Completely free. No account required. Works offline.</strong></p>
    <p><a class="go big" href="/app/">Open Huddle Board</a></p>
    <p class="small">Built for 6U–8U and divisions where the coach is on the field.
      5-on-5, 6-on-6 or 7-on-7. Open in your browser or
      <a href="#install">add it to your home screen</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <img class="shot" src="~/img/play.png" alt="A play on the tablet: routes and players marked by shape, color and spoken name" width="800">
</section>

<section class="points">
  <article>
    <h2>Show the play. Then show their job.</h2>
    <p>Watch the team run the play, with the ball following each exchange. Tap a
      player to step through their job while everyone else holds still. Teach it
      at practice, then give a quick reminder in the huddle.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>Blue and orange make sides clear</h2>
    <p>Young players can mix up left and right. Colors stay the same whether
      you're standing beside the kids or facing them.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>A job they can recognize</h2>
    <p>A shape, a color and a name you can say out loud help each kid find their
      spot. Familiar route words carry over from one play to the next.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>Ready when the team is</h2>
    <p>Get it ready at home, then use it with no signal at the field. Your setup
      stays on the tablet, and app updates wait for your tap between plays.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="feature">
  <img class="shot" src="~/img/deck.png" alt="The coach's deck of plays, with run, pass and situation filters" width="800">
  <div>
    <h2>Your team's plays, ready to call</h2>
    <p>Start with four calls: a run, a quick pass, a third-down play and a goal-line
      play. Choose more from the library, give them names your kids remember, and
      keep the plays you want for this week together.</p>
    <p>Draw your own plays and preview them before practice. The designer checks
      your drawings using the same rules as the included library. Print your deck
      as a reference sheet, or pass a setup file to an assistant coach's tablet.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="install">
  <h2>The whole app is free.</h2>
  <p class="lede">The play library, drawing tools, animation and printing are all
    included. No subscription, paid upgrade or payment details. Open it and start
    getting ready for practice.</p>
  <p>Huddle Board is also open source under the MIT license. You can keep a copy,
    adapt it for your team, or pass it on to next season's coach. See the
    <a href="https://github.com/crawfordjustin/huddle-board">source on GitHub</a>
    or <a href="/about">read how it started on a real sideline</a>.</p>
  <p><a class="go big" href="/app/">Open Huddle Board — it's free</a></p>
</section>

@* Installing has to start from /app/: that page carries the manifest, so an
   install from here would only be a bookmark for the website. *@
<section class="install" id="install">
  <h2>Get ready for the field</h2>
  <p class="lede">Add Huddle Board to your home screen for quick access at practice
    and on game day. Set it up once at home on wifi, then use it offline on the sideline.</p>
  <div class="steps">
    <article>
      <h3>Android tablet or phone</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>In <b>Chrome</b>, tap <a href="/app/">Open Huddle Board</a>. Install from the
          app itself, not from this page.</li>
        <li>Tap the <b>⋮</b> menu, then <b>Install app</b> or <b>Add to Home screen</b>.</li>
        <li>Open it from the new <b>Huddle Board</b> icon from now on, not from a Chrome tab.</li>
      </ol>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>iPad or iPhone</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>In <b>Safari</b>, tap <a href="/app/">Open Huddle Board</a>.</li>
        <li>Tap <b>Share</b> (the square with the arrow), then <b>Add to Home Screen</b>.</li>
        <li>Tap <b>Add</b>, and open it from the icon from now on.</li>
      </ol>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Laptop, Chrome or Edge</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Open <a href="/app/">Huddle Board</a>.</li>
        <li>Click the install icon at the right end of the address bar, or the menu, then
          <b>Install Huddle Board</b>.</li>
        <li>It opens in its own window and has its own icon.</li>
      </ol>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="small">Open it once more with a signal after installing, so it is ready
    offline. When a new version is out, the app offers <b>Update ready</b> on the deck. It
    never updates in the middle of a play. To remove it, press and hold the icon and
    uninstall, the same as any app. Everything you set up stays on that tablet.</p>
</section>
